#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# find_instance

#% text
# `find_instance(cond, x)` gives one point satisfying `cond` as `[[x -> v]]`; `find_instance(cond, [x, y])` for several variables; `[]` when there is none.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With one variable the condition is reduced by `reduce` and a root or a simple number inside an interval is taken.

#% item
# With several variables the equations are solved by `solve` and the unknowns left free are set to 0.

#% item
# Real polynomial conditions with an inequality (or the domain `reals`) take a sample point of the cylindrical algebraic decomposition; `find_instance(cond, vars, reals, n)` lists up to `n` points of a finite solution set.

#% item
# `find_instance(cond, vars, integers)` and `find_instance(cond, vars, integers, n)`: Pell equations `x^2 - D y^2 == 1` through the powers of the fundamental unit, bounded problems by bounds from the real decomposition and a complete search of the box, others by a search of the integer points with coordinates up to 60 in absolute value. Every point is checked exactly; when none is found the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A root:

#% cell
find_instance(x^2 == 4 and x > 0, x)
#% output
#= [[x -> 2]]

#% text
# A point of an interval:

#% cell
find_instance(x^2 < 4 and x > 1, x)
#% output
#= [[x -> 3/2]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Two equations:

#% cell
find_instance(x + y == 3 and x - y == 1, [x, y])
#% output
#= [[x -> 2, y -> 1]]

#% text
# An underdetermined system:

#% cell
find_instance(x + y == 3, [x, y])
#% output
#= [[x -> 3, y -> 0]]

#% text
# No solution:

#% cell
find_instance(x^2 < 0, x)
#% output
#= []

#% text
# All the points of a finite real set:

#% cell
find_instance(x^2 + y^2 == 1 and x == 2*y + 1, [x, y], reals, 5)
#% output
#= [[x -> -3/5, y -> -4/5], [x -> 1, y -> 0]]

#% text
# A solution of a Pell equation in a range:

#% cell
find_instance(x^2 - 3*y^2 == 1 and 10 < x and x < 100, [x, y], integers)
#% output
#= [[x -> 26, y -> 15]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `reduce` gives all the solutions:

#% cell
reduce(x^2 < 4 and x > 1, x)
#% output
#= 1 < x and x < 2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `reduce`, `solve`
